## Usage

### Basic
::::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="AttachmentTrayAttachmentTrayDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import type { AiAttachment, AiAttachmentFile } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/ai-elements'
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const attachments = ref<AiAttachment[]>([
    { kind: 'image', id: 'i1', url: 'https://picsum.photos/id/1015/400/300', name: 'canyon.jpg' },
    { kind: 'image', id: 'i2', url: 'https://picsum.photos/id/1043/400/300', name: 'shore.jpg', uploading: true, progress: 0.6 },
    { kind: 'file', id: 'f1', name: 'report.pdf', size: 240_000 },
    { kind: 'file', id: 'f2', name: 'uploading.zip', size: 1_200_000, uploading: true, progress: 0.4 },
  ])

  // The component never mutates the list: the host drops removed and cancelled ids.
  function drop(id: string) {
    attachments.value = attachments.value.filter(item => item.id !== id)
  }

  function onOpen(file: AiAttachmentFile) {
    // Opening or downloading the file is up to the host.
  }
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxAttachmentTray
      :attachments="attachments"
      removable
      @remove="drop"
      @cancel="drop"
      @open="onOpen"
    />
  </template>
---
::::

### Best Practices

- Set `removable` in a composer and drop the `id` on `remove` and `cancel`; keep sent messages read-only.
- Give an in-flight attachment both `uploading: true` and `progress` (0–1); without `progress`, no progress shows.
- Handle `open`; otherwise clicking a file chip does nothing.
- On non-English surfaces, override every text prop and `sizeFormatter`; `previousText` and `nextText` are visible text.
- Resize thumbnails with `--tx-attachment-tray-thumb-size` rather than overriding the component's internal classes.

## API Reference

### TxAttachmentTray

#### Props

| Name | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `attachments` | `AiAttachment[]` | — | Images and files in one list. Required. |
| `removable` | `boolean` | `false` | Shows remove buttons; cancel-upload buttons don't depend on it. |
| `previewTitle` | `string` | `'Preview'` | Viewer title when the image has no `name`. |
| `previousLabel` | `string` | `'Previous image'` | Accessible name of the previous button. |
| `nextLabel` | `string` | `'Next image'` | Accessible name of the next button. |
| `previousText` | `string` | `'Prev'` | Visible text of the previous button. |
| `nextText` | `string` | `'Next'` | Visible text of the next button. |
| `closeLabel` | `string` | `'Close'` | Accessible name of the preview's close button. |
| `removeLabel` | `string` | `'Remove attachment'` | Accessible name of remove buttons. |
| `cancelLabel` | `string` | `'Cancel upload'` | Accessible name of cancel-upload buttons. |
| `sizeFormatter` | `(bytes: number) => string` | — | Formats file sizes; defaults to whole bytes under 1 KB, then KB/MB/GB with one decimal. |

#### Events

| Name | Payload | Description |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `remove` | `(id: string)` | Fires when remove is clicked. |
| `cancel` | `(id: string)` | Fires when cancel-upload is clicked. |
| `open` | `(attachment: AiAttachmentFile)` | Fires when a file chip is clicked; images open the built-in viewer. |

### TxAttachmentChip

#### Props

| Name | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `attachment` | `AiAttachment & { kind: 'file' }` | — | The file attachment to show. Required. |
| `removable` | `boolean` | `false` | Shows the remove button; the cancel-upload button doesn't depend on it. |
| `removeLabel` | `string` | `'Remove attachment'` | Accessible name of the remove button. |
| `cancelLabel` | `string` | `'Cancel upload'` | Accessible name of the cancel-upload button. |
| `sizeFormatter` | `(bytes: number) => string` | — | Formats the file size; defaults to the same format as `TxAttachmentTray`. |

#### Events

| Name | Payload | Description |
|------|---------|-------------|
| `remove` | `(id: string)` | Fires when remove is clicked. |
| `cancel` | `(id: string)` | Fires when cancel-upload is clicked. |
| `open` | `(attachment: AiAttachment & { kind: 'file' })` | Fires when the chip body is clicked. |

### CSS Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `--tx-attachment-tray-thumb-size` | `72px` | Side length of an image thumbnail. |

- The variable is not declared on the root, so setting it on the component or any ancestor takes effect.

## Overview

- `kind: 'image'` items go to the image grid and `kind: 'file'` items to file chips; pass both in one `attachments` array.
- Each file renders as a `TxAttachmentChip`; the tray forwards `removable`, `removeLabel`, `cancelLabel`, and `sizeFormatter` to it.
- An `uploading` attachment always has a cancel button: images draw a progress ring, file chips show a percentage and a thin progress bar.
- An image's remove or cancel button sits inside the thumbnail's top-right corner; it appears on hover or keyboard focus and stays visible on touch screens.
- Clicking an image opens the built-in viewer, which emits nothing; with focus in the viewer, ← / → page through images, and focus moves to the opposite button at either end.
- Until an image arrives, the viewer holds its place, shaped by the attachment's `width` / `height` when given and otherwise like the last image that loaded, and shows a shimmering placeholder there once 150 ms have passed.
- An image that fails to load shows a placeholder icon in both the thumbnail and the viewer; the same URL is not retried, and a new `url` loads again.

## Technologies

- Thumbnails pin their own `img` margin and size, so an article's typography cannot shift them; the viewer is mounted on `<body>`, outside the article's styles.
- The viewer is the same internal component as `TxImageGallery`'s lightbox, shown here as a centered `TxModal` panel, and its styles live in the `image-gallery` sheet. The on-demand style plugin loads it; when importing styles by hand, add `@talex-touch/tuffex/image-gallery/style.css` and `@talex-touch/tuffex/modal/style.css`.
